# Coverage gap G5 (research/kernel-audit/coverage.md section 2): a lid with the block's footprint, its
# bottom drafted 0.1deg about its middle line and its ends drafted about the block's top, then the
# block added under it. The lid's dipped corner sits 5 theta^2 = 1.52 LINEAR off the block's side.
# The part is valid (1500.218 mm3), but today the kernel refuses the block with ZeroThickness near
# (10, 2.5, 9.9956) (G5a: imprint stretch samples, forge-bool boolean.rs:4227-4244). At 0.05deg it
# refuses with UntouchedOnOther (G5b: nearly_flush's NEAR cap, ssi.rs:66); at 0.2deg it builds.
shared W = 10
shared H = 10
shared T = 5
param bottom.a = 0.1deg
param ends.a = -0.1deg
sketch lidp(on: offset(xy, H)) {
  r = rect(corner: (0, 0), size: (W, W))
  m = pt(0, W / 2)
}
lid = extrude(lidp, T)
half = plane(at: lidp.m, normal: lidp.r[1].dir, x: lidp.r[0].dir)
bottom = draft(lid.start, angle: a, neutral: half)
ends = draft(lid.side(lidp.r[0]), lid.side(lidp.r[2]), angle: a, neutral: lidp.plane)
sketch foot(on: offset(lidp.plane, 0 - H)) {
  s = rect(corner: (0, 0), size: (W, W))
}
block = extrude(foot, H)
